# MSBuild / VSTO project files are owned by the Visual Studio project system,
# not by a generic formatter. Prettier treats them as plain XML and reflows
# attributes purely on print-width; it cannot maintain MSBuild/VSTO semantics
# (ProjectTypeGuids, import ordering, RunSettingsFilePath, NuGet-restore targets).
# Visual Studio rewrites these files to its own single-line shape on every save,
# so letting Prettier format them produces perpetual churn as the two tools
# undo each other. Per CLAUDE.md, formatters must not touch project files
# (csharpier is .cs-only by design). Leave *.csproj / *.props / *.targets to VS.
*.csproj
*.props
*.targets
